{"abstract":"Dataset development for automatic summarisation systems is notoriously English-oriented. In this paper we present the first large-scale non-English language dataset specifically curated for automatic summarisation. The document-summary pairs are news articles and manually written summaries in the Danish language. There has previously been no work done to establish a Danish summarisation dataset, nor any published work on the automatic summarisation of Danish. We provide therefore the first automatic summarisation dataset for the Danish language (large-scale or otherwise). To support the comparison of future automatic summarisation systems for Danish, we include system performance on this dataset of strong well-established unsupervised baseline systems, together with an oracle extractive summariser, which is the first account of automatic summarisation system performance for Danish. Finally, we make all code for automatically acquiring the data freely available and make explicit how this technology can easily be adapted in order to acquire automatic summarisation datasets for further languages.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Varab, Daniel","Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382282"],"event":{"acronym":"LREC","title":"International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automatic summarisation","Danish language dataset","Document summary pairs","Non English summarisation","Unsupervised baseline systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danewsroom a large scale danish summarisation dataset","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551562/DaNewsroom.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382282","identifier":[{"id":"85096566522","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-448828b4-0d75-48e9-9841-9ad54c8b2727"],"keyword":["Automatic summarisation","Danish language dataset","Document-summary pairs","Non-English summarisation","Unsupervised baseline systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C2B0A2AC442EEE30EB96179C97A6001A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.lrec-1.831/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.lrec-1.831.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551562/DaNewsroom.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"varabpau","last":"Varab","name":"Varab, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"6731-6739","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 12th Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC 2020)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-448828b4-0d75-48e9-9841-9ad54c8b2727"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DaNewsroom: A Large-scale Danish Summarisation Dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382282","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The current state-of-the-art in neural graphbased parsing uses only approximate decoding at the training phase. In this paper aim to understand this result better. We show how recurrent models can carry out projective maximum spanning tree decoding. This result holds for both current state-of-the-art models for shiftreduce and graph-based parsers, projective or not. We also provide the first proof on the lower bounds of projective maximum spanning tree, DAG, and digraph decoding.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383896"],"event":{"acronym":"NAACL HLT","title":"Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Approximate Decoding","Neural Graph based Parsing","Projective Maximum Spanning Tree","Recurrent Models","Shift Reduce Parsers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recurrent models and lower bounds for projective syntactic decoding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/N19-1022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383896","identifier":[{"id":"85085556018","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b4ca3ad8-e91f-444d-990b-57eb0b7b7510"],"keyword":["Approximate Decoding","Neural Graph-based Parsing","Projective Maximum Spanning Tree","Recurrent Models","Shift-Reduce Parsers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9BD5941EAA81565570C4FAA650D6BC02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/N19-1022","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84929187/watermarked_NAACL2019_NatalieSchluter.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/N19-1022.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/n19-1022","pages":"251-260","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2019 Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies","volume":"Volume 1 (Long and Short Papers)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085556018"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b4ca3ad8-e91f-444d-990b-57eb0b7b7510"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Recurrent models and lower bounds for projective syntactic decoding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383896","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Danish is a North Germanic language spoken principally in Denmark, a country with a long tradition of technological and scientific innovation. However, the language has received relatively little attention from a technological perspective. In this paper, we review Natural Language Processing (NLP) research, digital resources and tools which have been developed for Danish. We find that availability of models and tools is limited, which calls for work that lifts Danish NLP a step closer to the privileged languages. Dansk abstrakt: Dansk er et nordgermansk sprog, talt primært i kongeriget Danmark, et land med stærk tradition for teknologisk og videnskabelig innovation. Det danske sprog har imidlertid været genstand for relativt begrænset opmærksomhed, teknologisk set. I denne artikel gennemgår vi sprogteknologi-forskning, -ressourcer og -værktøjer udviklet for dansk. Vi konkluderer at der eksisterer et fåtal af modeller og værktøjer, hvilket indbyder til forskning som løfter dansk sprogteknologi i niveau med mere priviligerede sprog.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","Plank, Barbara","Derczynski, Leon","Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384150"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danish language","Digital resources","Natural Language Processing NLP","Technological innovation","linguistic tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the lacunae of danish natural language processing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551035/W19_6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384150","ids":["itu-c4ada506-a42e-465f-88b3-4007eccdc03e"],"keyword":["Danish language","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","digital resources","linguistic tools","technological innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A4CAA5EB28526A34F399035105BB77BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/W19-6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551035/W19_6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Søeborg","key":"kirkedalpau","last":"Kirkedal","name":"Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789179299958"],"issn":["17366305"],"pages":"356-362","publisher":"Linköping University Press","series":"NEALT (Northern European Association of Language Technology) Proceedings Series","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Nordic Conference of Computational Linguistics (2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c4ada506-a42e-465f-88b3-4007eccdc03e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Lacunae of Danish Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384150","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Exposure science provides fundamental knowledge at the interface between chemicals and other stressors in the environment including workplaces and consumer goods, and their negative effects on humans and ecosystems. This knowledge is crucial for our understanding of the complex human-environment-stressor interactions in support of a safe and sustainable future. Education and training of the various exposure science topics yields important expertise required for regulatory risk assessment, for product evaluations and for scientific advances essential for health and environmental science, as well as market and societal demands. The European Chapter of the International Society of Exposure Science (ISES Europe) has initiated and reported on exposure science requirements as input for building a European Exposure Science Strategy, collated from all relevant stakeholders and the scientific community. In support of building this strategy, various topics to strengthen exposure science in Europe were discussed at the first ISES Europe workshop in 2018 along a set of thematic themes addressing: 1.data repositories and analytics, 2. regulatory exposure assessment, 3. exposure data production and monitoring, 4. building partnerships and collaboration, 5. exposure assessment methods and tools and 6. exposure science education and communication. To contribute to ISES Europe’s objectives, a working group focusing on exposure science in education, training and communication was established, with an overarching aim to anchor exposure science in academic research and education, and to establish a defined career pathway for graduates. An important building block in the European Exposure Science Strategy is to develop a tiered education/training scheme with ECTS equivalent points/certificates, and to identify ways to support and promote existing courses with focus on exposure science. The preliminary analysis, objectives and expected outcomes will be presented in this talk, alongside the action plan to achieve these outcomes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Connolly, Alison","Fantke, Peter","von Goetz, Natalie","Bessems, Jos","Schlüter, Urs","Dudzina, Tatsiana","Bruinen de Bruin, Yuri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352827"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-22","place":"Kaunas, lt","start":"2019-08-18","title":"Joint Meeting of the International Society of Exposure Science and the International Society of Indoor Air Quality and Climate","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Ireland","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Commission","ExxonMobil","Federal Institute for Occupational Safety and Health","Federal Office of Public Health","Flemish Institute for Technological Research","University of Galway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"establishing exposure science in education","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203309712/Connolly_2019a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352827","ids":["dtu-a1baca36-05d1-46a1-b911-032d6582a6aa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E81019A09968D85E0D48D98AE5C1A4F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203309712/Connolly_2019a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ie","key":"university of galway","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Galway","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Sustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Sustainability, Society and Economics, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"federal office of public health","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Federal Office of Public Health","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"flemish institute for technological research","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Flemish Institute for Technological Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"federal institute for occupational safety and health","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Federal Institute for Occupational Safety and Health","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"exxonmobil","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"ExxonMobil","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"be","key":"european commission","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Commission","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alison","key":"connollypau","last":"Connolly","name":"Connolly, Alison","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"fantkepau","last":"Fantke","locid":"5ba443c7-8e07-4435-9946-883e7f5f1ff7","name":"Fantke, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7148-6982","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"vongoetzpau","last":"von Goetz","name":"von Goetz, Natalie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jos","key":"bessemspau","last":"Bessems","name":"Bessems, Jos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Urs","key":"schlüterpau","last":"Schlüter","name":"Schlüter, Urs","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatsiana","key":"dudzinapau","last":"Dudzina","name":"Dudzina, Tatsiana","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"bruinendebruinpau","last":"Bruinen de Bruin","name":"Bruinen de Bruin, Yuri","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"326-326","status":"p","title":"Book of abstract of Joint Meeting of the International Society of Exposure Science and the International Society of Indoor Air Quality and Climate 27th Annual Meeting"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a1baca36-05d1-46a1-b911-032d6582a6aa"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Establishing exposure science in education","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352827","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In Europe, exposure science is closely related to various regulations. However, recent scientific advances face difficulties in finding their way into regulatory common practices. This is a major driver for the European Chapter of the International Society of Exposure Science (ISES Europe) to initiate developing an urgently needed «European Exposure Science Strategy» by soliciting exposure scientists from all relevant stakeholder communities. In building this European strategy for exposure science, we will focus on the following set of six overarching objectives: (i) To build a European Programme and related infrastructure to generate, assess, exchange, and communicate experimental and model-based exposure information; (ii) To advance exposure science with focus on closing existing knowledge gaps, building science-based and operational data and methods, fostering integration and interaction of disciplines involved in exposure science; (iii) To provide guidance and recommendations for exposure assessment in science and policy; (iv) To foster the inclusion of realistic exposure information in various regulatory and non-regulatory assessment and management frameworks and related decision-making processes; (v) To strengthen the impact of exposure science on human health and environmental policies; and (vi) To support trans-agency and trans-institutional coordination, education, and engaging a broader European stakeholder community including triggering. These objectives will be addressed through establishing dedicated working groups from the wider European exposure science community to foster a focused and consolidated effort that will ultimately provide guidance for improving and increasing the use of exposure science in in European regulation and practice. Initial focus will be on objectives with highest priority and capacity within the related stakeholder community.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fantke, Peter","von Goetz, Natalie","Bessems, Jos","Connolly, Alison","Schlüter, Urs","Dudzina, Tatsiana","Bruinen de Bruin, Yuri"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352352"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-22","place":"Kaunas, lt","start":"2019-08-18","title":"Joint Meeting of the International Society of Exposure Science and the International Society of Indoor Air Quality and Climate","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Ireland","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Commission","ExxonMobil","Federal Institute for Occupational Safety and Health","Federal Office of Public Health","Flemish Institute for Technological Research","National University of Ireland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward a european exposure science strategy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203309472/Fantke_2019i.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352352","ids":["dtu-a01edb86-d93e-4e28-838d-34bc5a63b069"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-26A99102BA1CA4B2BB2B9BABEE258C9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203309472/Fantke_2019i.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Man