{"abstract":"The recent years have seen a revival of interest in textual entailment, sparked by i) the emergence of powerful deep neural network learners for natural language processing and ii) the timely development of large-scale evaluation datasets such as SNLI. Recast as natural language inference, the problem now amounts to detecting the relation between pairs of statements: they either contradict or entail one another, or they are mutually neutral. Current research in natural language inference is effectively exclusive to English. In this paper, we propose to advance the research in SNLI-style natural language inference toward multilingual evaluation. To that end, we provide test data for four major languages: Arabic, French, Spanish, and Russian. We experiment with a set of baselines. Our systems are based on cross-lingual word embeddings and machine translation. While our best system scores an average accuracy of just over 75%, we focus largely on enabling further research in multilingual inference.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Agic, Zeljko","Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381262"],"event":{"acronym":"LREC","title":"International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cross lingual methods","natural language inference","test data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"baselines and test data for cross lingual inference","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83054422/1704.05347.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381262","identifier":[{"id":"85059911148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-00ef2199-9e6d-4a52-ab71-0e2a1256cfdf"],"keyword":["cross-lingual methods","natural language inference","test data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A11A20392D7F887B56CEF4FA0C885F6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83054422/1704.05347.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1704.05347.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeljko","key":"agicpau","last":"Agic","name":"Agic, Zeljko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9791095546009"],"pages":"3890-3894","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Eleventh International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC 2018)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059911148"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-00ef2199-9e6d-4a52-ab71-0e2a1256cfdf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Baselines and test data for cross-lingual inference","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381262","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we provide empirical evidence based on a rigourously studied mathematical model for bi-populated networks, that a glass ceiling within the field of NLP has developed since the mid 2000s.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383109"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","title":"Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Empirical evidence","Mathematical modeling","NLP glass ceiling","bi populated networks","mid 2000s trends"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the glass ceiling in nlp","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83851772/D18_1301.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383109","identifier":[{"id":"85081754611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7dde9a38-5fa6-4b38-9310-e3a19778c6b8"],"keyword":["NLP glass ceiling","bi-populated networks","empirical evidence","mathematical modeling","mid-2000s trends"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2E78961054969F3895C5948D06D43FC2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/D18-1301","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83851772/D18_1301.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781948087841"],"pages":"2793-2798","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081754611"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7dde9a38-5fa6-4b38-9310-e3a19778c6b8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The glass ceiling in NLP","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383109","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Consider two competitive machine learning models, one of which was considered state-of-the art, and the other a competitive baseline. Suppose that by just permuting the examples of the training set, say by reversing the original order, by shuffling, or by mini-batching, you could report substantially better/worst performance for the system of your choice, by multiple percentage points. In this paper, we illustrate this scenario for a trending NLP task: Natural Language Inference (NLI). We show that for the two central NLI corpora today, the learning process of neural systems is far too sensitive to permutations of the data. In doing so we reopen the question of how to judge a good neural architecture for NLI, given the available dataset and perhaps, further, the soundness of the NLI task itself in its current state.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie","Varab, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382050"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","title":"Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dataset Dependency in NLP Systems","Machine Learning Model Sensitivity","Natural Language Inference NLI","Neural Architecture Evaluation","Training Data Permutations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"when data permutations are pathological the case of neural natural language inference","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83851876/D18_1534.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382050","identifier":[{"id":"85081714907","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3537ffda-b314-4d03-9d75-51826032fba2"],"keyword":["Dataset Dependency in NLP Systems","Machine Learning Model Sensitivity","Natural Language Inference (NLI)","Neural Architecture Evaluation","Training Data Permutations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-571CAF11ADC4F26381437A862FA18F4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/D18-1534","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83851876/D18_1534.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"varabpau","last":"Varab","name":"Varab, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781948087841"],"pages":"4935-4939","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081714907"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3537ffda-b314-4d03-9d75-51826032fba2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"When data permutations are pathological: the case of neural natural language inference","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382050","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"There are some important problems in the evaluation of word embeddings using standard word analogy tests. In particular, in virtue of the assumptions made by systems generating the embeddings, these remain tests over randomness. We show that even supposing there were such word analogy regularities that should be detected in the word embeddings obtained via unsupervised means, standard word analogy test implementation practices provide distorted or contrived results. We raise concerns regarding the use of Principal Component Analysis to 2 or 3 dimensions as a provision of visual evidence for the existence of word analogy relations in embeddings. Finally, we propose some solutions to these problems.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382761"],"event":{"acronym":"NAACL HLT","title":"Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evaluation Methodologies","Principal component analysis","Randomness in Embeddings","Word Analogy Tests","Word Embeddings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the word analogy testing caveat","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/N18-2039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382761","identifier":[{"id":"85082451247","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6356946a-983f-4070-a953-9210a0585e34"],"keyword":["Evaluation Methodologies","Principal Component Analysis","Randomness in Embeddings","Word Analogy Tests","Word Embeddings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1428E2D39F902A716ADEF88C9CA58B7E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83851736/N18_2039.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/N18-2039","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/N18-2039","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/n18-2039","eisbn":["9781948087292"],"pages":"242-246","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","subtitle":"Volume 2 (Short Papers)","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082451247"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6356946a-983f-4070-a953-9210a0585e34"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Word Analogy Testing Caveat","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382761","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses some central caveats of summarisation, incurred in the use of the ROUGE metric for evaluation, with respect to optimal solutions. The task is NPhard, of which we give the first proof. Still, as we show empirically for three central benchmark datasets for the task, greedy algorithms empirically seem to perform optimally according to the metric. Additionally, overall quality assurance is problematic: there is no natural upper bound on the quality of summarisation systems, and even humans are excluded from performing optimal summarisation.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383657"],"event":{"acronym":"EACL","title":"Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Greedy algorithms","NP hard","Quality assurance","ROUGE metric","Summarisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the limits of automatic summarisation according to rouge","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83029693/E17_2007.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383657","identifier":[{"id":"85021690990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a390c866-4177-4348-a38e-082424b6fe59"],"keyword":["Greedy algorithms","NP-hard","Quality assurance","ROUGE metric","Summarisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-516D5440081F340323561D5D8B9AB6C9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://www.aclweb.org/anthology/E17-2007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83029693/E17_2007.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781945626340"],"pages":"41-45","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 15th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a390c866-4177-4348-a38e-082424b6fe59"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The limits of automatic summarisation according to ROUGE","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383657","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Universal Dependencies incur a high cost in computation for unbiased system development. We propose a 100% empirically chosen small subset of UD languages for efficient parsing system development. The technique used is based on measurements of model capacity globally. We show that the diversity of the resulting representative language set is superior to the requirements-based procedure.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schluter, Natalie","Agic, Zeljko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384835"],"event":{"acronym":"NODALIDA","title":"Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Empirical methods","Language subset selection","Model capacity","Parsers","Universal Dependencies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"empirically sampling universal dependencies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/W/W17/W17-0415.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384835","identifier":[{"id":"85080746927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f2a0ef40-9a8c-466a-8274-0198d84440a2"],"keyword":["Empirical methods","Language subset selection","Model capacity","Parsers","Universal Dependencies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4991387A4536401A160ED42CBF3C4510"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82097189/schluter2017_sampling.preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/W/W17/W17-0415.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"