{"abstract":"In dependency parsing, jackknifing taggers is indiscriminately used as a simple adaptation strategy. Here, we empirically evaluate when and how (not) to use jackknifing in parsing. On 26 languages, we reveal a preference that conflicts with, and surpasses the ubiquitous ten-folding. We show no clear benefits of tagging the training data in cross-lingual parsing.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Agic, Zeljko","Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383992"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","title":"Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross lingual parsing","Dependency parsing","Empirical Evaluation","Jackknifing","Ten fold cross validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how not to train a dependency parser the curious case of jackknifing part of speech taggers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/P17-2107","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383992","identifier":[{"id":"85040607451","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ba9c82be-0413-4d81-bf2c-75fad794a84b"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual parsing","Dependency parsing","Empirical evaluation","Jackknifing","Ten-fold cross-validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5521BBD723A5212A034EF4D38776EC7D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/P17-2107","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82097242/agic2017_how.preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeljko","key":"agicpau","last":"Agic","name":"Agic, Zeljko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/p17-2107","eisbn":["9781945626760"],"pages":"679-684","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 55th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040607451"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ba9c82be-0413-4d81-bf2c-75fad794a84b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How (not) to train a dependency parser: The curious case of jackknifing part-of-speech taggers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383992","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
